      "subtitle": "英语二小作文 · 2010 真题",
      "questionText": "47. Directions:\nYou have just come back from the U.S. as a member of a Sino-American cultural exchange program. Write a letter to your American colleague to\n1) express your thanks for his/her warm reception;\n2) welcome him/her to visit China in due course.\nYou should write about 100 words on ANSWER SHEET 2.\nDo not sign your own name at the end of the letter. Use “Zhang Wei” instead.\nDo not write your address. (10 points)",
      "questionImages": [],
      "referenceText": "Dear Jane,\n\nThank you very much for receiving me, a delegate of the Sino-American cultural exchange program, during my visit to the United States. Your warm reception made me feel at home. You kindly explained American customs to me, which helped me get over culture shock quickly and gain a deeper understanding of American culture. I really appreciate everything you have done for me.\n\nIn return, I would like to invite you to visit China so that I can reciprocate your hospitality. I promise you a fantastic visit, through which you may gain a deep insight into Chinese culture. I look forward to your visit.\n\nYours sincerely,\nZhang Wei"
