      "subtitle": "英语二小作文 · 2014 真题",
      "questionText": "47. Directions:\nSuppose you are going to study abroad and share an apartment with John, a local student. Write him an email to\n1) tell him about your living habits, and\n2) ask for advice about living there.\nYou should write about 100 words on the ANSWER SHEET.\nDo not use your own name. Use “Li Ming” instead.\nDo not write your address. (10 points)",
      "questionImages": [],
      "referenceText": "Dear John,\n\nI am glad that you will be my roommate during my overseas study and cannot wait to meet you. Before I move in, I think it is necessary for us to reach a basic understanding about each other's living habits.\n\nAs a typical Chinese, I keep regular hours and prefer simple, healthy meals. I also like to keep the room tidy and clean. In addition, I enjoy cooking Chinese dishes at home and hope you will tolerate the occasional spicy smell during preparation. There must also be some special living rules to be respected in your country. Could you explain them to me in advance? I look forward to your early reply.\n\nYours,\nLi Ming"
