      "subtitle": "英语二小作文 · 2019 真题",
      "questionText": "47. Directions:\nSuppose Professor Smith asked you to plan a debate on the theme of city traffic.\nWrite him an email to\n1) suggest a specific topic with your reasons, and\n2) tell him about your arrangements.\nYou should write about 100 words on the ANSWER SHEET.\nDo not use your own name. Use “Li Ming” instead.\nDo not write your address. (10 points)",
      "questionImages": [],
      "referenceText": "Dear Professor Smith,\n\nThank you for trusting me to arrange the debate. I am writing to suggest a topic for it.\n\nI suggest “Is Traffic Jam Caused by Inadequate Transport Infrastructure or Poor Management?”. It is debatable because it involves two major causes of traffic paralysis. Moreover, given that urban planning and public policies are taught this semester, the argument will deepen students' understanding of their courses. Finally, it touches on issues students care about, such as shared bikes, which will get them to think and talk.\n\nThe debate will be held in the school hall from 6:00 p.m. to 8:00 p.m. on Friday. I look forward to your response.\n\nYours sincerely,\nLi Ming"
